<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  Er-Con Technologies theme fonts.

    Headings  Archivo        a grotesque; squared, engineered, holds up at size
    Body      Source Sans 3  a humanist text face; set for reading, not for display

  A third face does the work the theme cannot hold: IBM Plex Mono carries every
  value - money, dates, proposal numbers, percentages, data labels. OOXML has
  only two theme font slots, so figure runs name Plex Mono outright. See
  _build/set-typefaces.py, which applies that rule by the run's own text.

  All three are SIL Open Font License 1.1, so they may be embedded in a document.
  Turn embedding on: Word or PowerPoint, Preferences (Mac) or File > Options
  (Windows) > Save > Embed fonts in the file. Embed the WHOLE font, not just the
  characters used, or text the recipient types falls back.

  Nothing in the templates names a font except the two slots below. Changing the
  brand face is one edit here and in the templates' own theme part.
-->
<a:fontScheme xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" name="Er-Con Technologies">
  <a:majorFont><a:latin typeface="Archivo"/><a:ea typeface=""/><a:cs typeface=""/></a:majorFont>
  <a:minorFont><a:latin typeface="Source Sans 3"/><a:ea typeface=""/><a:cs typeface=""/></a:minorFont>
</a:fontScheme>
